cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, data or the accompanying manuscript, please cite
  this repository together with the journal article once it is published.
title: >-
  Insomnia TCM Mining — Reproducible Experiment Package for Apriori
  Association Rule and Complex Network Analysis of Insomnia Traditional
  Chinese Medicine Prescriptions
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Junhua
    family-names: Li
    email: junhua.li@example.org
  - given-names: Gilja
    family-names: So
    email: gilja.so@example.org
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-05-16"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-github-user>/insomnia-tcm-mining"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end, single-command reproducible pipeline (eleven Python
  scripts, a Makefile and a docx-js paper builder) that derives all the
  numerical results, eight figures and eight tables of the accompanying
  manuscript from two minimum-necessary CSV inputs containing only the
  fields prescription_id and herb. The package is intended to allow any
  third party to independently verify the reported numbers via a single
  `make all` command.
keywords:
  - traditional Chinese medicine
  - insomnia
  - data mining
  - Apriori
  - association rules
  - complex network analysis
  - Louvain community detection
  - reproducible research
